# Architecture Patterns & Conventions

## MVVM Pattern Implementation

### ViewModels
- All ViewModels extend `ChangeNotifier` from Provider package
- Located in [lib/viewmodels/](mdc:lib/viewmodels)
- Handle business logic, API calls, and state management
- Use `notifyListeners()` to update UI when state changes

Example: [home_view_model.dart](mdc:lib/viewmodels/home_view_model.dart) manages home screen state

### Views (Screens)
- Located in [lib/screens/](mdc:lib/screens)
- Stateless or Stateful widgets that consume ViewModels
- Use `Provider.of<ViewModel>(context)` to access state
- Focus only on UI rendering and user interactions

Example: [home_view.dart](mdc:lib/screens/home_view.dart) displays the main screen

### Models
- Data classes in [lib/models/](mdc:lib/models)
- Include JSON serialization methods (`toJson()`, `fromJson()`)
- Primary models: [situation.dart](mdc:lib/models/situation.dart), [user_mode.dart](mdc:lib/models/user_mode.dart)

## Provider Setup

Configured in [main.dart](mdc:lib/main.dart) using `MultiProvider`:
```dart
MultiProvider(
  providers: [
    ChangeNotifierProvider(create: (_) => AuthProvider()),
    ChangeNotifierProvider(create: (_) => HomeViewModel()),
    // ... other providers
  ],
  child: MaterialApp(...)
)
```

## Service Layer

Services in [lib/services/](mdc:lib/services) handle external integrations:
- [auth_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/auth_service.dart) - Firebase Authentication
- [notification_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/notification_service.dart) - Push notifications
- [item_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/item_service.dart) - Firestore CRUD operations
- [situation_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/situation_service.dart) - Situation management

## Widget Organization

### Reusable Components
- [lib/widgets/](mdc:lib/widgets) contains reusable UI components
- Organized by functionality (Buttons, forms, etc.)
- [custom_list_tile.dart](mdc:lib/widgets/custom_list_tile.dart) - Custom list items
- [reusable_buttons.dart](mdc:lib/widgets/Buttons/reusable_buttons.dart) - Common button patterns

### Naming Conventions
- Views end with `_view.dart` (e.g., `home_view.dart`)
- ViewModels end with `_view_model.dart`
- Services end with `_service.dart`
- Widgets use descriptive names reflecting their purpose

## State Management Pattern

1. **UI Events** → Trigger ViewModel methods
2. **ViewModel** → Calls appropriate Service
3. **Service** → Handles Firebase/external operations
4. **ViewModel** → Updates state and calls `notifyListeners()`
5. **UI** → Rebuilds automatically via Provider
